{%- comment -%}
  What happens after you enter.

  The purchase is not the end of the relationship in a prize competition — it is
  the start of a wait. A customer who does not know what that wait looks like
  has an unanswered question at the moment they are deciding to pay, and no
  reason to come back afterwards.

  Every line is derived from data the store actually holds, or from mechanics
  the storefront already commits to elsewhere. Nothing here promises a message,
  a document or a record that the business has no way to send:

  - the draw date is shown only when custom.draw_at is set
  - the entry-number line appears only when settings.entry_numbers_issued is on,
    because nothing currently allocates entry numbers (see docs/QA.md)

  DATES THAT HAVE PASSED ARE NOT SHOWN.

  "Entries close on Tue 1 Sep" printed beside a working Enter button in late
  September is worse than silence: it states a deadline the page is visibly
  ignoring, and invites the entrant to believe entries have stopped when
  Shopify will still sell them one. Entries stop when inventory runs out, not
  on a date, so a date that has been and gone describes nothing and is
  dropped.

  Parameters:
    product  (required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign draw_at = product.metafields.custom.draw_at.value
  assign closing_at = product.metafields.custom.closing_at.value

  assign now_epoch = 'now' | date: '%s' | times: 1

  assign closing_is_future = false
  if closing_at != blank
    assign closing_epoch = closing_at | date: '%s' | times: 1
    if closing_epoch > now_epoch
      assign closing_is_future = true
    endif
  endif

  assign draw_is_future = false
  if draw_at != blank
    assign draw_epoch = draw_at | date: '%s' | times: 1
    if draw_epoch > now_epoch
      assign draw_is_future = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

<div class="next-steps">
  <h2 class="next-steps__heading h4">{{ 'products.competition.next_heading' | t }}</h2>
  <ol class="next-steps__list" role="list">
    <li class="next-steps__step">
      {%- render 'icon', icon: 'check-circle', size: 16 -%}
      <span>{{ 'products.competition.next_confirmation' | t }}</span>
    </li>

    {%- if settings.entry_numbers_issued -%}
      <li class="next-steps__step">
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'ticket', size: 16 -%}
        <span>{{ 'products.competition.next_numbers' | t }}</span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if closing_is_future -%}
      <li class="next-steps__step">
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'clock', size: 16 -%}
        <span>
          {%- assign closes_text = closing_at | date: '%a %-d %b' -%}
          {{- 'products.competition.next_closes' | t: date: closes_text -}}
        </span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if draw_is_future -%}
      <li class="next-steps__step">
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'trophy', size: 16 -%}
        <span>
          {%- assign draw_text = draw_at | date: '%a %-d %b' -%}
          {{- 'products.competition.next_draw' | t: date: draw_text -}}
        </span>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    <li class="next-steps__step">
      {%- render 'icon', icon: 'shield', size: 16 -%}
      <span>{{ 'products.competition.next_published' | t }}</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>
